# Example htpasswd file for nginx basic auth.
# Do NOT commit real credentials. To generate a password entry locally, run:
#
#   # install apache2-utils (Debian/Ubuntu) or httpd-tools (RHEL/CentOS)
#   htpasswd -c ./nginx/.htpasswd tulip
#
# The command will prompt for a password and create `./nginx/.htpasswd`.
# Copy that file to the same path in the host before starting the proxy.

# Example (do not use this literal entry):
# tulip:$apr1$randomsalt$abcdefghijklmnopqrstuv
